{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252491-wizened-s-mien-in-the-2e","id":1252491,"title":"Wizened's Mien in the 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-08T05:38:15-07:00","id":1252491,"title":"Wizened's Mien in the 2e","content":"I was reading the part about Wizened in the changeling 2 edition corebook and apparently they dumped the idea of Wizened as homemade cyborgs but i don't got it what they are now, they also don't look like the thin or/and small men, women and NBs of the previous edition they look like they are just absolutely perfect and obssesed with their craft<br /> <br /> Anyone could explain how Wizened's Mien look like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T06:35:07-07:00","id":1252498,"title":"","content":"The Wizened have always been one of the less physically remarkable seemings; the cues to build on are mostly marks of their work turned up to at least an eight or a nine and given a touch of the weird. 2e differs from 1e in its emphasis on <i>experience</i> over diminishment \u2014 the headspace of the Hatters is &quot;you've been doing what you do for a very long time and you know the job inside and out.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T06:55:00-07:00","id":1252500,"title":"","content":"Thank you for answering and yeah it makes sense, i decided to re-read the descriptions of some of the Wizened and i re-read the description of the Artist Wizened<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The tiny, gnarled woman has splotches across her paper-white skin that might be ink or might be veins. Her eyes are a vivid, unearthly blue. She is never<br /> without her watercolors and can paint Arcadia from<br /> memory. Some Lost wish she wouldn\u2019t. </div> </div> </div>And now i can totally understand what you meant, they look like people who done the job for soo much time and in such a great way that parts of the job merged with them, like the artist might have ink in their veins and the color of the eyes might look similar with one the color she uses frequently and i think what complements that interpretation is the description of the leechfinger Wizened<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other fae often mistake this changeling for a<br /> mortal. They look normal. Too normal. Everything about<br /> them is designed to appear as average as possible, from their<br /> height to their eye color to the mid-alto pitch of their voice.<br /> Everything, that is, except for their long, spidery fingers </div> </div> </div>All the parts that changed are parts focused in their job in that case steal life throught their fingers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T08:53:37-07:00","id":1252519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queer Snake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1252491-wizened-s-mien-in-the-2e?p=1252500#post1252500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the parts that changed are parts focused in their job in that case steal life throught their fingers</div> </div> </div> </div>Also: Leechfingers are what they eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}